# ============================================================================
# MonieNaija V1 — SUPER_ADMIN recovery/revocation ceremony configuration template
# ============================================================================
# Companion documents:
#   - docs/deployment/V1-SUPER-ADMIN-RECOVERY-RUNBOOK-01.md (follow it exactly)
#   - docs/V1/V1-SECURITY-SUPER-ADMIN-RECOVERY-01-REPORT.md (implementation report)
#   - docs/V1/V1-ADMIN-ADMINISTRATOR-GOVERNANCE-DECISIONS-01.md §3 (approved design)
#
# RULES:
#  - Every variable below EXISTS in src/config/environment.ts and
#    src/authorization/workforce-configuration.ts — nothing here is invented.
#  - This file contains ONLY references, identifiers, and PUBLIC keys. A private
#    key NEVER belongs in any env file: the recovery/revocation private key lives
#    only in the offline signing custodian's ceremony environment, structurally
#    separate from this application's deployment configuration and from the
#    bootstrap ceremony's own key (A2_BOOTSTRAP_JWKS_JSON) — never reuse one for
#    the other.
#  - Sections marked PRODUCTION-REQUIRED must be set for a real deployment that
#    intends to ever be able to run this ceremony.
#  - Sections marked RECOVERY WINDOW are relevant only while a ceremony is in
#    progress; A2_RECOVERY_ENABLED may be left `true` permanently (unlike the
#    one-shot A2_BOOTSTRAP_ENABLED window) because every individual statement is
#    still separately signed, scoped, time-boxed, and single-use — see the
#    runbook §7 for the organizational decision on whether to also gate this
#    flag behind a change-controlled window for defense in depth.
#  - This template assumes the WORKFORCE AUTHENTICATION and BOOTSTRAP blocks in
#    docs/deployment/config/v1-workforce-bootstrap.env.template are already
#    configured — recovery is additive to that configuration, not a replacement
#    for it.
# ============================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SUPER_ADMIN RECOVERY / REVOCATION (PRODUCTION-REQUIRED to ever use this ceremony)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Master switch, independent of A2_WORKFORCE_ENABLED and A2_BOOTSTRAP_ENABLED.
# When false (the default), the consuming endpoint fails closed with
# "Recovery disabled" regardless of any other configuration or caller authority.
A2_RECOVERY_ENABLED=false

# REQUIRED when A2_RECOVERY_ENABLED=true. Must equal the --audience value passed
# to scripts/generate-revocation-statement.ts for every statement this deployment
# is expected to accept. Keep this distinct from A2_BOOTSTRAP_AUDIENCE so a
# bootstrap statement can never be replayed against the recovery endpoint or
# vice versa (the two statement schemas and operations differ, but a distinct
# audience is cheap, explicit defense in depth).
A2_RECOVERY_AUDIENCE=monienaija-v1-super-admin-recovery

# Trust for the recovery statement-signing key(s). PRODUCTION-REQUIRED when
# A2_RECOVERY_ENABLED=true (startup fails closed otherwise: "A2_RECOVERY_JWKS_JSON:
# at least one trusted key required when recovery enabled"). REPLACE the empty
# array with the envSnippet.A2_RECOVERY_JWKS_JSON printed by
# `npm run recovery:statement` (it contains the PUBLIC key only — see the
# runbook §3-4). The JWK 'environment' field must equal NODE_ENV, exactly like
# the bootstrap key's environment field.
#
# STRUCTURAL INVARIANT: this MUST be a key set independent of A2_BOOTSTRAP_JWKS_JSON
# — never point both variables at the same key material. The approved design
# (V1-ADMIN-ADMINISTRATOR-GOVERNANCE-DECISIONS-01.md §3) requires the revocation
# ceremony's trust chain to be structurally separate from the creation ceremony's,
# even though both ceremonies reuse the same generic RS256 verification code.
#
# Example shape (single line, kid pattern [A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9_.:-]*):
#   A2_RECOVERY_JWKS_JSON=[{"kid":"<kid>","kty":"RSA","n":"...","e":"AQAB","alg":"RS256","use":"sig","environment":"production"}]
A2_RECOVERY_JWKS_JSON=[]

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PREREQUISITE REMINDER — not new variables, already required by the pre-existing
# workforce/bootstrap configuration, repeated here only because the recovery
# ceremony depends on them being correctly set:
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   A2_WORKFORCE_ENABLED=true           (recovery consumption is a WORKFORCE_SESSION
#                                        route; it fails closed if the workforce
#                                        plane itself is disabled)
#   A2_FINANCE_ROLES_JSON               (must include the ADMINISTRATOR role —
#                                        see v1-workforce-bootstrap.env.template)
#   A2_WORKFORCE_RATE_LIMITS_JSON       (must include the "finance-role-administration"
#                                        category, which this endpoint reuses rather
#                                        than requiring a new rate-limit category)
#
# The recovery ceremony does NOT require A2_BOOTSTRAP_ENABLED=true to CONSUME a
# revocation statement. A2_BOOTSTRAP_ENABLED only needs to be (re-)opened for the
# SEPARATE, subsequent step of naming a successor SUPER_ADMIN (§8 of the runbook)
# — revocation and replacement-bootstrap are two independent ceremonies composed
# together, not one combined operation.
